<?nvs
// A temporary directory, as a program: the one thing this fixture shows is
// what it does *not* contain — there is no cleanup line at the bottom.
//
// [ADR 0131](/docs/decisions/0131.md)
// is the whole story. `Core\IO::temporaryDir` hands back a directory under
// the root Novis owns (§ 2), the program writes into it as it likes, and
// when the script ends the runtime deletes it (§ 3) — after the last user
// code, off the request path, and without ever throwing. So a fixture that
// tidied up after itself would be pinning nothing: the interesting claim is
// that walking off the end of this file is enough, which
// `a_finished_scripts_temporary_dir_is_gone_from_the_owned_root` asserts
// from outside once the script is over.
//
// Compare `examples/files.nvs`, which removes what it made. That one is
// about `Core\IO`'s four verbs, and its `removeDir` is there so the fixture
// leaves nothing behind. Here leaving something behind is the point, and the
// runtime is what takes it away. There is deliberately nothing to opt into:
// no `temporaryFile`, no per-call persist, and the one escape hatch —
// `[debug] keep_temporary` (§ 5) — belongs to the operator, not to the
// program, because a script that could exempt its own files could be made to
// hoard them.
//
// The line this prints is frozen by an exact check in a goal record under
// `data/goals/`; the source is not.

string $dir = Core\IO::temporaryDir();
string $note = Core\Path::join($dir, 'note.txt');

Core\IO::write($note, "hello from a temporary\n");
echo 'wrote and read: ', Core\Str::trim(Core\IO::readText($note)), "\n";

// And that is the end of the program. `$dir` still exists as this line runs;
// it does not exist by the time the process is gone.
